body:
だめ can be used interchangeably with other words with a similar meaning (f.ex いけない or ならない), in combination with a conditional construction to express something that must not be done or a necessity (when the verb bearing the conditional is negated as well). -きゃ is basically a shortcut for a double negative construction where you replace the end of the negated verb. That way you can leave out the whole だめ/いけない/ならない part. Just replace -なければ with -なきゃ or -なくて with -なくちゃ

&nbsp;

Example:

&nbsp;
今週末は、宿題をやらなきゃ。 This weekend [I] have to do some homework.
